{
  "version": 1,
  "_why": "Machine-readable gates. Deliberately NOT global pytest totals: a total moves every time anyone adds a test, so pinning it teaches people to bump the number rather than to look. What is pinned here is BEHAVIOUR \u2014 which adversarial cases must be blocked, which acceptance scenarios must exist and pass, that no forbidden adapter call happens, and that the migration chain is consistent. Changing anything under `safety` is a safety change and the runner refuses it without an explicit acknowledgement.",
